WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.320
The number one game would be [the University of] Southern California game of 1979.

2
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.920
LSU had a great team.

3
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.920
Southern California had a great team.

4
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:17.360
A lot of the fellows off both those teams went directly to professional football.

5
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:22.580
The stadium was sold out, here, and it was an exciting thing.

6
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:28.480
John Robinson was the coach at Southern California and Charlie McClendon was the coach at LSU.

7
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.500
And as I said, they had . . . Both of them had great teams.

8
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.000
There were two great teams on the field.

9
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.880
That was an exciting time and it was,

10
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:57.560
as I commented a lot of times—in a day when people are falling all over themselves in a lot of ways to step on other people and get where they want and out-maneuver and out-finagle other people in a lot of ways—for three hours that night,

11
00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.900
everybody was together.

12
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:03.140
It was a moment.

13
00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.360
Not really pulling for one team or the other.

14
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:12.540
They were just pulling for the game and excitement and the thrill of the moment.

15
00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:18.320
It was really . . . It was really a high point in all of the times I spent in Tiger Stadium.
